BND-09: round the total duration to the nearest second instead of truncating it

OptionsHandler copies 5.3.0's floor((EndDate - StartDate)*86400 +
(EndTime - StartTime)*86400), and SimulationOptions::totalDurationMs() (used
after the dates are set through the API) floors the combined serials as 5.2.4
did. Both often come out one second short, so the run stops at END - 1 s and
the last reporting period is never saved. Add 0.5 before each floor.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-09_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/SimulationOptions.hpp b/src/engine/core/SimulationOptions.hpp
index c076ed1..97402cb 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/SimulationOptions.hpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/SimulationOptions.hpp
@@ -823,12 +823,12 @@ struct SimulationOptions {
 
     /** @brief Total simulation duration in milliseconds (legacy TotalDuration).
      *  @details Returns the legacy-exact value stored by the INP options
-     *  handler when available; otherwise falls back to flooring the combined
+     *  handler when available; otherwise falls back to rounding the combined
      *  serial difference to whole seconds (mirroring legacy swmm5.c:3198-3200
      *  as closely as the combined representation allows). */
     double totalDurationMs() const {
         if (total_duration_ms >= 0.0) return total_duration_ms;
-        return std::floor((end_date - start_date) * 86400.0) * 1000.0;
+        return std::floor((end_date - start_date) * 86400.0 + 0.5) * 1000.0;
     }
 };
 
